.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt SSHD.CONF 5
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sshd.conf
.Nd limits of the SSH server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/sshd.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm sshd
reads
.Nm
once, when it starts, through the file server; changing the file takes
effect at the next boot.
It is not OpenSSH's
.Pa sshd_config :
the keywords differ and there are only these.
.Pp
Each line is a keyword and one value, separated by spaces or tabs.
Blank lines and lines whose first word begins with
.Ql #
are ignored.
Each keyword may appear once; values are decimal whole numbers.
An absent keyword keeps its default.
.Bl -tag -width "login-grace-time seconds"
.It Cm port Ar number
The TCP port to listen on, 1 to 65535.
Default 22.
.It Cm max-connections Ar number
Connections served at once, authenticated or not, 1 to 4.
Default 4.
Each connection has one session.
Four is what the kernel's tables serve: 48 pipes, of which the file server
channels and the server's own streams take 24 and each shell session
without a terminal 5 (a fifth such session would be refused its shell).
.It Cm login-grace-time Ar seconds
How long a connection may take to authenticate before it is dropped,
1 to 3600.
Default 30.
.It Cm idle-timeout Ar seconds
How long a connection may pass with no traffic in either direction and no
output from its command before it is closed, 1 to 604800.
Default 1800.
.It Cm max-auth-tries Ar number
Refused authentication attempts before the connection is dropped, 1 to
100.
Default 6.
.El
.Pp
Without the file every value is its default, and
.Nm sshd
says so on the console.
The operator image installs the file with the default values.
.Ss When every connection is taken
While
.Cm max-connections
connections are open,
.Nm sshd
takes no new one.
A further client's TCP handshake is still completed by the network stack,
up to the listener's backlog (which equals
.Cm max-connections ),
but a connection over the limit is refused at the transport boundary at
once: reset with no banner and no session slot, with
.Ql SSH GLOBAL REFUSED
recorded on the console.
Stock
.Nm ssh
reports the reset and exits with status 255 rather than waiting out its
.Cm ConnectTimeout .
.Pp
A source address holds at most two unauthenticated connections at once;
further pre-authentication connections from the same source are refused
the same way, with
.Ql SSH PREAUTH REFUSED ... reason=source-limit
on the console.
Authenticated sessions do not consume that allowance, but still count
against
.Cm max-connections .
.Pp
Separately, every session needs a file server channel; there are ten.
Four connections take at most four channels and their commands' spares,
and a session whose shell ends its commands leaves none held when it ends
.Pq Xr absd-sh 1 .
A command left running because the server had to kill its shell
.Pq Ql SSH SESSION END ... forced=true
keeps its channel out of use until it ends.
A session that finds none free is refused: a shell request fails,
and stock
.Nm ssh
prints
.Dq shell request failed on channel 0
and exits with status 255; a command is not started, and the client gets
.Dq sshd: NAME: no free file server slot
and status 126.
The channels come back as those commands end.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
At every start
.Nm sshd
prints on the console, and writes to
.Pa /var/log/sshd :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sshd: port 22, at most 4 connections, login grace 30 s, idle
timeout 1800 s, 6 authentication tries (/etc/sshd.conf)
.Ed
.Pp
A malformed file (an unknown keyword, including OpenSSH's such as
.Cm Port ,
a keyword twice, a missing or extra value, a value out of range, a byte
that is not printable ASCII, more than 4096 bytes) is refused: the console
names the file, the line, and the reason,
.Nm sshd
does not start, and the boot fails.
No default replaces a value the operator wrote.
See
.Xr afterboot 8
for fixing it.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr network.conf 5 ,
.Xr afterboot 8
